# kubernetes/apps

Workloads, one directory per module, reconciled by the `apps` Flux Kustomization.

Every module here is **generic platform machinery**, not an application you run
for its own sake. Your actual apps go in one of two places:

- **in this repo** — add a directory following the same shape (namespace,
  workload, NetworkPolicy, VPA, kustomization) and list it in
  `kustomization.yaml`;
- **in their own repo** — onboard it as a tenant, so it deploys from its own git
  history with its own CI. See
  `kubernetes/clusters/{{ cluster_name }}/tenants/README.md`.

## Modules in this cluster

| Module | What it is | Disable by |
|---|---|---|
| `authentik` | SSO/identity provider (OIDC + ForwardAuth) | removing the entry — but also un-wire Grafana OIDC and every `authentik-auth` middleware reference |
| `registry-cache` | pull-through container registry cache for CI | removing the entry |
| `vm-ingress` | pattern for fronting off-cluster hosts with cluster ingress | removing the entry |
{%- if vpn_tailscale %}
| `tailnet-dns` | split-horizon resolver for tailnet clients | removing the entry + dropping the Split-DNS nameserver from the tailnet policy |
{%- endif %}
{%- if git_backend == 'gitlab_selfhosted' %}
| `gitlab-runner` | shared, non-privileged CI runner (untagged jobs) | removing the entry |
| `gitlab-runner-privileged` | trusted CI runner (root + DinD) for this repo's own deploys | removing the entry |
| `gitlab-runner-reaper` | GCs leaked runner job pods and their per-job Secrets | removing the entry |
{%- endif %}

Each module has a README covering what it does, when you want it, what to
configure and how to remove it.
{%- if git_backend == 'gitlab_selfhosted' %}

Register the privileged runner as described in `gitlab-runner-privileged/README.md`
§ The registration scope IS the security boundary.
{%- endif %}

The shape a new module follows, and the gates it has to pass, are in
`.claude/skills/cluster-development/references/add-k8s-app.md`.
